actors: Agent runner | This app | OPA | Alice

step: The agent asks to delete old reports
msg: Agent runner -> This app: purge_reports
text: The runner makes the call with the agent's own token, like any other
  tool. Nothing about the request says it is special.

step: The gateway asks the policy
msg: This app -> OPA: may it?
text: Same question as lab 08, same document: the agent, the capabilities on
  its token and the tool with its arguments.

step: The policy says yes, and flags it
msg: OPA -> This app: allow + approval
note: OPA: capability says approval
text: The capability for `purge_reports` carries `"approval": "required"`.
  The policy copies that into its answer as `requires_approval`. It has not
  said "run it". It has said "run it once a person agrees".

step: The app queues a request and answers 202
msg: This app -> Agent runner: 202 pending
note: This app: request + trace id kept
text: The row records the agent, its sponsor, the tool and a fingerprint of the
  exact arguments. Nothing has been deleted.

step: The agent waits and asks how it is getting on
msg: Agent runner -> This app: poll the request
text: The runner polls once a second. While the request is pending the answer
  holds no token.

step: Alice sees the request in the queue and approves it
msg: Alice -> This app: approve
note: This app: may_decide, then a 60s token
text: Alice is the agent's sponsor, so she is allowed to decide. Approving
  mints a token that lives for a minute. The queue never shows it.

step: The next poll hands the agent its token
msg: This app -> Agent runner: approval token
text: Only the agent that asked can collect it. A denial would have come back
  here too, with no token.

step: The agent repeats the call with the token
msg: Agent runner -> This app: purge + token
note: This app: token tied to this call
text: The call carries the approval id and token. The app checks that the token
  is live and belongs to this agent, this tool and these arguments, then spends
  it.

step: The work runs, and the audit log tells the whole story
msg: This app -> Agent runner: deleted 3
note: This app: held, approved, run
text: One trace id covers the first request, Alice's decision and the run. Spent
  tokens are wiped, so the same approval can't be used twice.
